  "release_gates": [
    "No production traffic in tests.",
    "No raw private address, recipient, witness, private key, proof secret, or production credential material in public fixtures.",
    "ADDRESS_HASH remains discouraged and unsafe-by-default.",
    "Proof functions accept envelope or proof policy, not raw address as the primary public interface.",
    "Calcite remains deferred until activation gates are met.",
    "ZK hooks remain proof-input/verifier-hook readiness, not audited circuits.",
    "AMT compatibility is an adapter boundary, not an AMT paper chapter.",
    "Third-party source/data licenses remain separate from code licensing.",
    "Practical API responses must not reflect submitted postal codes or accept raw address and recipient fields.",
    "Public-source sync may create conformance adapters, but only an independently supplied Ed25519 public key and valid signature may activate approved evidence.",
    "Cross-language place-name transformation remains disabled until country-specific source, holdout, signature, and runtime evidence is approved.",
    "Official aliases and official romanizations must outrank generated transliterations; translation alone must never create an official-name claim.",
    "Same-script place-name ambiguity must defer unless country and administrative hierarchy context identify a unique supported candidate.",
    "Place-name holdout reports contain country and administrative-hierarchy aggregates only; raw address or recipient vectors are prohibited.",
    "L4 delivery-area evidence must never be promoted to an L5 delivery-point decision.",
    "L5 requests accept only delivery-point commitments and signed carrier decisions; carrier disagreement stops as conflict.",
    "Expired postal adapters must disappear from runtime capability and evaluation without requiring a restart.",
    "Postal operations reports accept aggregate-safe correction timestamps only and never mutate country capability state."
  ],
